                        "entry_id": "a1f8ec66-0476-37c7-aaab-6cb66fd6e84c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A device used to measure the intensity of a smell"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9621973a-6295-48a8-aa89-c7f65b2176cc",
                                "sense_id": "16d5b248-6012-37d0-bbae-f11e3db4ebed",
                                "text": "Most of the odorometers now in use have been designed so that measured quantities of odorized gas are mixed with air furnished by an electrically driven blower."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d6f120f-2fb6-4aa1-bdf0-51011e03d27a",
                                "sense_id": "16d5b248-6012-37d0-bbae-f11e3db4ebed",
                                "text": "The types of detectors of importance are the odorometer, titrators, and the odotron."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "524541c3-57ea-4335-86a9-f26c60eab8d2",
                                "sense_id": "16d5b248-6012-37d0-bbae-f11e3db4ebed",
                                "text": "On the quiet side, sanitation engineers like Gordon Fair tremendously improved both the testing and treatment of wastewater, bringing in chlorination, increasing aeration, and even introducing odorometers (not to be confused with odometers)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
